WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Think about the pencil sitting on your desk.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.300
It seems incredibly simple, right?

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.600
Wood, graphite, a bit of metal, an eraser.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.000
Yet it is entirely impossible for any single human being

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.700
on the face of the earth to make one from scratch.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.100
Let's start with the wood.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.400
Cedar harvested from Oregon requires heavy machinery.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.200
You need steel saws, meaning steel mills.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.900
You need heavy rope, requiring hemp processing.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.000
Building saws demands mining iron ore,

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.100
extraction equipment, railroads, and massive industrial plants

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.900
just to make the logger's tools.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.400
Ultimately, millions of individuals across the planet

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.500
have physically contributed microscopic amounts of labor

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.700
to manufacture this tiny object.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.700
This brings up a massive behavioral puzzle.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.700
None of these millions of interacting workers

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.800
share a language or culture, and almost none of them

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.700
actually care about building a pencil.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.900
The miner in Sri Lanka and the lumberjack in Oregon

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:57.800
aren't coordinating.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.700
They are simply exchanging their isolated highly specialized

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.700
know-how for the specific wages, goods, and services

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.000
they personally desire.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.700
The free market's price system acts

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.700
as an automatic communication network.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.100
It directs raw materials, labor and creative energy

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.500
across the globe faster and more efficiently

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.500
than any human designer ever could.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.200
True human progress and the creation

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.300
of the miracles we take for granted every single day

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.400
relies entirely on allowing this system to work.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.000
It requires an unwavering faith

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.800
in the spontaneous, voluntary cooperation of free people.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.100
Not a plan. Permission. Free people, allowed to build, make your money go further. Count me in. freemarketabundance.com
